Changes made: nothing is copied verbatim. Its bug-bounty validation rules were
condensed, reworded and re-aimed at verifying, investigating and reviewing code, and
its redaction patterns and denylist scan were rewritten as a shell script. The rules
drawn on are its statistical-sample, marker, body-diff and shell-loop rules, the
layer-ordering trap, exploit-completion, the mid-engagement capture-and-diff rule,
subagent scope inheritance, the coverage closure in engine/closure.py, the redaction in
engine/verifier.py, the identifier scan and skill linter in scripts/, the false-positive
benchmark in eval/, and the workflow and invisible-text classes of hunt-cicd and
hunt-llm-ai.

